<span>, some with ties to firms under national security sanctions, to buy a=
nd handle Nvidia chips.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia=
,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>In other instances, the chips don=
=E2=80=99t actually need to make it into China at all. Southeast Asia has b=
ecome a hub of what=E2=80=99s called offshore computing, a legal practice i=
n which America=E2=80=99s advanced A.I. chips, which can be used to develop=
 and operate new cutting-edge A.I. models, are used in data centers housed =
in countries like Thailand, Vietnam or Malaysia. Their computing power, tho=
ugh, is still routed to companies based in China.</span></p><p style=3D"fon=
t:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D=
"font-weight:700">Blowback</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px geor=
gia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>News of Huang=E2=80=99s affair =
has rocketed around the globe, generating shock waves from Taiwan to Silico=
n Valley to Washington. U.S. lawmakers have asked him to appear for a close=
d-door briefing. A Nvidia spokesman said the company had worked =E2=80=9Cto=
 help government and our partners halt any would-be smugglers while serving=
 the critical market of lawful customers that help America win worldwide.=
=E2=80=9D</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#=
333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>A lot is still unknown, not just about what exac=
tly happened but also about how it is going to play out in terms of A.I. po=
licy. Huang has been among the strongest opponents of restrictions on A.I. =
He has also opposed restrictions on chip sales and argued for allowing Nvid=
ia to sell its products more freely. It=E2=80=99s harder for him to make th=
at argument now.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;=
color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>At the same time, lawmakers who have long=
 been critical of the tech industry see the affair as an opening. Senator E=
lizabeth Warren, a Democrat who has sponsored legislation that would tighte=
n oversight on chip exports and crack down on the ecosystem that gave rise =
to Megaspeed, has called for legislation =E2=80=9Cto keep our advanced A.I.=
 technology out of China=E2=80=99s hands.=E2=80=9D</span></p><p style=3D"fo=
nt:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The ups=
hot is that Jensen Huang=E2=80=99s affair could well alter U.S.-China relat=
ions and, perhaps, the course of the A.I. race between the world=E2=80=99s =
two largest economies. The implications go far beyond what China=E2=80=99s =
spymasters may have had in mind when they allegedly gave Alice Huang her as=
signment.</span></p><div style=3D"margin:0 auto;max-width:600px;width:100%"=
